# ── Build OUTPUT. Regenerated from the master by nf-build-tools; never tracked.
#    Deleting a SHIP folder loses nothing the generator cannot rebuild.
# Anchored with a leading / so they match at the REPO ROOT ONLY. Without the
# anchor, SHIP-2026-*/ also swallowed nf-build-tools/ship/SHIP-2026-08-30f/ --
# the template bundle every build grafts its heads from. That MUST be tracked.
/SHIP-2026-*/
/_SHIP-*.tgz
/_ship*.tgz
/_build/

# ── Snapshots of the tools. Superseded 9 Sep 2026: the tools themselves are now
#    tracked below, and the six patches that existed ONLY inside the 3 Sep
#    tarball were extracted to patches/_not-in-build-chain/ before this was set.
nf-build-tools-*.tgz
nf-build-tools/faq/nf-faq-tools-*.tgz

# ── Generated, read by nothing (51 MB computed-style dump)
nf-build-tools/ship/base-styles.json

# ── Working scratch and machine noise
_archive/
.tmpcheck/
_compare/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
.DS_Store
*.log

# ── Media lives on the CDN (_CDN-UPLOAD-SAFE -> nofilter-shared), not in git
*.mp4
*.mp3
